nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}} — {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

Question asked off camera: {{inputs.question}}
The answer to land: {{inputs.answer}}
Closing line: {{inputs.cta}}
Casting note: {{inputs.presenter}}

Cast ONE person who plausibly walks down that street and write a 3-beat interview: beat 1 is the surprised first reaction to the question, beat 2 is the real answer, beat 3 names the brand as an aside rather than a slogan.

`actor` must pin identity down hard enough to repeat: apparent age, build, hair, face details, exact outerwear including colour and fabric, and the specific stretch of street with named things in it.

`master_frame_prompt` is a still-image prompt for the establishing frame of this person standing on that street, mid-answer. Describe the person, their clothing, the street and the light — no camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.

For each of the 3 shots write:
- `frame_prompt`: an EDIT instruction on the master frame. Always start with "Same person, same hair, same clothes, same street." then change only expression, head angle and framing.
- `motion_prompt`: what happens in the 5 seconds AFTER that frame — delivery only. Include the spoken line in double quotes.
- `line`: just the spoken words, at most 12 words so it fits in 5 seconds.

`on_screen_text`: the first caption is the question in quotes, then one caption per remaining beat, at most 6 words each.
